#. Translators: Spoken description of the list of ways silence can be measured, on the silence removal settings page. Peak and RMS are the names of the two methods.
#: UI/Silence.cs:14
msgid ""
"Peak follows the loudest sample in each analysis window and reacts to brief "
"sounds. RMS averages the window for steadier detection."
msgstr ""
"Peak sigue la muestra más alta en cada ventana de análisis y reacciona a "
"sonidos breves. RMS promedia la ventana para una detección más estable."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: which section of sound should end trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Silence.cs:19
msgid "Leading silent parts to trim"
msgstr "Partes silenciosas iniciales a recortar"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced setting that chooses which section of sound ends trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Silence.cs:21
msgid ""
"Use 0 to leave the beginning untouched or 1 to remove its initial silence. "
"Higher values continue trimming through additional sections of sound."
msgstr ""
"Usa 0 para no modificar el inicio o 1 para eliminar el silencio inicial. "
"Valores más altos continúan recortando a través de secciones adicionales de "
"sonido."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Silence.cs:23
msgid "Sound required before leading trim stops (seconds)"
msgstr "Sonido requerido antes de detener el recorte inicial (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced setting for how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Silence.cs:25
msgid ""
"Sound must stay above the threshold for this long before leading-silence "
"trimming stops. The default is 0.2 seconds."
msgstr ""
"El sonido debe mantenerse por encima del umbral durante este tiempo antes de "
"detener el recorte de silencio inicial. El valor predeterminado es 0.2 "
"segundos."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun.
#: UI/Silence.cs:27
msgid "Silent parts to trim after audio starts"
msgstr "Partes silenciosas a recortar después de que inicie el audio"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun. Minus one means every one of them.
#: UI/Silence.cs:29
msgid ""
"Use -1 to shorten every qualifying pause after sound begins, or 0 to leave "
"later pauses untouched."
msgstr ""
"Usa -1 para acortar cada pausa apta después de que comience el sonido, o 0 "
"para no modificar las pausas posteriores."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:31
msgid "Minimum inner silence length (seconds)"
msgstr "Duración mínima del silencio interno (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:33
msgid ""
"A quiet section after sound begins must last at least this long before it is "
"shortened."
msgstr ""
"Una sección silenciosa después de que comienza el sonido debe durar al menos "
"este tiempo antes de ser acortada."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:35
msgid "Pause to keep after trimmed silence (seconds)"
msgstr "Pausa a conservar tras el silencio recortado (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:37
msgid ""
"Keeps up to this much of a pause instead of removing it completely. The "
"default is 0.2 seconds."
msgstr ""
"Conserva hasta este tiempo de pausa en lugar de eliminarla por completo. El "
"valor predeterminado es 0.2 segundos."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Silence.cs:39
msgid "Detection window size (seconds)"
msgstr "Tamaño de la ventana de detección (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Silence.cs:41
msgid ""
"Sets how many seconds of samples are measured together. Larger windows are "
"steadier; smaller windows react faster. The default is 0.02."
msgstr ""
"Establece cuántos segundos de muestras se miden juntos. Ventanas más grandes "
"son más estables; ventanas más pequeñas reaccionan más rápido. El valor "
"predeterminado es 0.02."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the whole silence removal settings page, read when the page is opened.
#: UI/Silence.cs:56
msgid ""
"The basic controls decide how long and how quiet a pause must be before Luna "
"shortens it. Advanced controls treat silence at the beginning and after "
"sound starts separately."
msgstr ""
"Los controles básicos determinan qué tan larga y silenciosa debe ser una "
"pausa antes de que Luna la acorte. Los controles avanzados tratan por "
"separado el silencio del inicio y el posterior."

#. Translators: Title of the group holding the silence removal settings.
#. "FFmpeg silenceremove" is the name of the filter doing the work and is not translated.
#: UI/Silence.cs:64
msgid "Silence removal (FFmpeg silenceremove)"
msgstr "Eliminación de silencio (FFmpeg silenceremove)"

#. Translators: Label of the box for the shortest silence that will be trimmed, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Silence.cs:69
msgid "Minimum silence duration (seconds)"
msgstr "Duración mínima del silencio (segundos)"

#. Translators: Label of the box for the loudness under which sound counts as silence, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Silence.cs:71
msgid "Silence threshold"
msgstr "Umbral de silencio"

#. Translators: Label of the tick box that shows the rest of the silence removal settings.
#: UI/Silence.cs:75
msgid "Show advanced settings"
msgstr "Mostrar configuración avanzada"

#. Translators: Label of the list of ways silence can be measured, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Silence.cs:89
msgid "Detection mode"
msgstr "Modo de detección"

#. Translators: One of the two ways silence can be measured: by the loudest moment. This one answers quickly to speech.
#: UI/Silence.cs:93
msgid "Peak (fast reaction)"
msgstr "Peak (reacción rápida)"

#. Translators: One of the two ways silence can be measured: by the average loudness. This one is steadier. RMS is the usual name for it and can be left as it is.
#: UI/Silence.cs:95
msgid "RMS (smoother)"
msgstr "RMS (más suave)"

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the shortest silence that will be trimmed, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Silence.cs:115
msgid ""
"Raise this value to preserve more short pauses, or lower it to remove "
"briefer pauses. A quiet section is changed only after it lasts for the "
"entered number of seconds."
msgstr ""
"Aumenta este valor para conservar más pausas cortas, o redúcelo para "
"eliminar pausas más breves. Una sección silenciosa solo se modifica tras "
"durar el número de segundos ingresado."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the loudness under which sound counts as silence, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Silence.cs:119
msgid ""
"Enter a decibel value such as -30. A less negative value treats louder audio "
"as silence and removes more; a more negative value limits removal to very "
"quiet audio."
msgstr ""
"Introduce un valor en decibelios como -30. Un valor menos negativo trata el "
"audio más alto como silencio y elimina más; un valor más negativo limita la "
"eliminación al audio muy silencioso."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that shows the rest of the silence removal settings.
#: UI/Silence.cs:123
msgid ""
"Reveals separate controls for leading and later silence, the amount of each "
"pause to retain, and the method used to measure loudness."
msgstr ""
"Muestra controles independientes para el silencio inicial y posterior, la "
"cantidad de pausa a conservar y el método usado para medir la sonoridad."

#. Translators: Help text for the list of ways silence can be measured. Peak and RMS are the names of the two methods.
#: UI/Silence.cs:127
msgid ""
"Peak uses the loudest sample in each analysis window and responds to brief "
"sounds. RMS uses average energy, producing a steadier result that is less "
"affected by short spikes."
msgstr ""
"Peak utiliza la muestra más alta en cada ventana de análisis y responde a "
"sonidos breves. RMS utiliza la energía promedio, logrando un resultado más "
"estable y menos afectado por picos cortos."

#. Translators: Error message shown when the shortest silence to trim was typed as something other than a number, or as a negative one.
#: UI/Silence.cs:137
msgid "Minimum silence duration must be a non-negative number."
msgstr "La duración mínima del silencio debe ser un número no negativo."

#. Translators: Error message shown when the silence loudness threshold was typed as something other than a number.
#: UI/Silence.cs:143
msgid "Silence threshold must be a valid number."
msgstr "El umbral de silencio debe ser un número válido."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting needs a whole number.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Leading silent parts to trim".
#: UI/Silence.cs:158
msgid "{field} must be an integer value."
msgstr "{field} must be an integer value."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting cannot be negative.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Leading silent parts to trim".
#: UI/Silence.cs:165
msgid "{field} must be zero or greater."
msgstr "{field} must be zero or greater."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting accepts -1 but nothing lower.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Silent parts to trim after audio starts".
#: UI/Silence.cs:172
msgid "{field} must be -1 or greater."
msgstr "{field} must be -1 or greater."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting needs a number that is not negative.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Sound required before leading trim stops (seconds)".
#: UI/Silence.cs:180
msgid "{field} must be a non-negative number."
msgstr "{field} must be a non-negative number."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting that chooses which section of sound ends trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Silence.cs:270
msgid ""
"Use 0 to preserve the beginning or 1 to remove initial silence until "
"sustained sound is found. Values above 1 continue discarding audio through "
"additional non-silent sections."
msgstr ""
"Usa 0 para conservar el inicio o 1 para eliminar el silencio inicial hasta "
"encontrar un sonido sostenido. Los valores superiores a 1 continúan "
"descartando audio a través de secciones adicionales no silenciosas."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Silence.cs:273
msgid ""
"After initial trimming, sound must remain above the threshold for this many "
"seconds before Luna starts keeping it. The default is 0.2."
msgstr ""
"Tras el recorte inicial, el sonido debe permanecer por encima del umbral "
"durante este número de segundos antes de que Luna comience a conservarlo. El "
"valor predeterminado es 0.2."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun.
#: UI/Silence.cs:276
msgid ""
"Use -1 to shorten every qualifying pause after sound begins. Use 0 to "
"preserve later silence; positive values limit how many sections are removed."
msgstr ""
"Usa -1 para acortar cada pausa apta después de que comience el sonido. Usa 0 "
"para conservar el silencio posterior; los valores positivos limitan cuántas "
"secciones se eliminan."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:278
msgid ""
"A pause after sound begins must remain below the threshold for this many "
"seconds before Luna shortens it."
msgstr ""
"Una pausa después de que comience el sonido debe permanecer por debajo del "
"umbral durante este número de segundos antes de que Luna la acorte."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Silence.cs:280
msgid ""
"Enter how many seconds of a removed pause should remain, so words do not run "
"together. The default is 0.2."
msgstr ""
"Introduce cuántos segundos de una pausa eliminada deben conservarse, para "
"que las palabras no se junten. El valor predeterminado es 0.2."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Silence.cs:282
msgid ""
"Sets the span of audio used for each loudness measurement. Larger values "
"smooth sudden changes; smaller values react faster. The default is 0.02 "
"seconds."
msgstr ""
"Establece el intervalo de audio utilizado para cada medición de sonoridad. "
"Valores más grandes suavizan los cambios abruptos; valores más pequeños "
"reaccionan más rápido. El valor predeterminado es 0.02 segundos."

#. Translators: Help text used for any silence removal setting with no help text of its own.
#: UI/Silence.cs:285
msgid "Enter a numeric value, then press OK to apply it."
msgstr "Introduce un valor numérico y presiona Aceptar para aplicarlo."

#. Translators: Label of the list choosing whether the sleep timer ends after a length of time or when
#. the current track finishes.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:55
msgid "End the timer"
msgstr "Finalizar el temporizador"

#. Translators: The sleep-timer option that fires after a chosen length of time.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:58
msgid "After a length of time"
msgstr "Después de un intervalo de tiempo"

#. Translators: The sleep-timer option that fires when the current track finishes.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:60
msgid "At the end of the current track"
msgstr "Al final de la pista actual"

#. Translators: Label of the list of ready-made timer lengths.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:64
msgid "Length"
msgstr "Duración"

#. Translators: One ready-made timer length. {minutes} is a number of minutes.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:68
msgid "{minutes} minutes"
msgstr "{minutes} minutos"

#. Translators: Label of the list choosing what happens when the timer fires.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:80
msgid "When the timer fires"
msgstr "Cuando el temporizador se active"

#. Translators: Tick box that fades the volume down over the last seconds before the timer fires.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:90
msgid "Fade the volume out before firing"
msgstr "Atenuar el volumen antes de activar"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how many seconds the fade lasts.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:92
msgid "Fade length (seconds)"
msgstr "Duración de la atenuación (segundos)"

#. Translators: Button in the sleep-timer window that turns off a timer already running.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:158
msgid "Turn off timer"
msgstr "Desactivar temporizador"

#. Translators: Shown when a timed sleep timer is set to a length of zero.
#: UI/SleepTimerDialog.cs:235
msgid "Choose a length of at least one minute."
msgstr "Elige una duración de al menos un minuto."

#. Translators: Title used for a window of read-only text when the caller supplies none.
#: UI/TextInfoDialog.cs:13
msgid "Information"
msgstr "Información"

#. Translators: Title of the window offering to fetch the extra programs YouTube needs.
#: UI/YouTube/ComponentsDialog.cs:21
msgid "YouTube Components"
msgstr "Componentes de YouTube"

#. Translators: Message offering to fetch the extra programs YouTube needs. Playing and saving
#. videos cannot work without them, which is what it says.
#: UI/YouTube/ComponentsDialog.cs:26
msgid ""
"Playing and downloading YouTube videos needs some extra programs that are "
"not installed yet. Would you like to download them now?"
msgstr ""
"Reproducir y descargar vídeos de YouTube requiere algunos programas "
"adicionales que aún no están instalados. ¿Deseas descargarlos ahora?"

#. Translators: Button that agrees to fetch the extra programs YouTube needs.
#: UI/YouTube/ComponentsDialog.cs:30
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Sí"

#. Translators: Button that declines to fetch the extra programs YouTube needs.
#: UI/YouTube/ComponentsDialog.cs:33
msgid "No"
msgstr "No"

#. Translators: Title of the window showing the text an uploader wrote under a YouTube video.
#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:36
msgid "Video description"
msgstr "Descripción del video"

#. Translators: Label before the box that shows the text written under a video.
#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:40
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descripción"

#. Translators: Button that saves the description as a plain-text (.txt) file.
#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:49
msgid "Export to text (.txt)..."
msgstr "Exportar a texto (.txt)..."

#. Translators: Button that saves the description as a web page (.html) file.
#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:51
msgid "Export to web page (.html)..."
msgstr "Exportar como página web (.html)..."

#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:125
msgid "Text files (*.txt)|*.txt"
msgstr "Archivos de texto (*.txt)|*.txt"

#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:132
msgid "Web pages (*.html)|*.html"
msgstr "Páginas web (*.html)|*.html"

#. Translators: Title of the window that asks where to save a video's description.
#: UI/YouTube/DescriptionDialog.cs:158
msgid "Save description"
msgstr "Guardar descripción"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding the address a saved link points at.
#. Translators: Heading of the favourites list column holding the address of each saved link.
#: UI/YouTube/FavoriteEditDialog.cs:35 UI/YouTube/FavoritesDialog.cs:33
msgid "Link"
msgstr "Enlace"

#. Translators: Message shown when a YouTube address names a video and a playlist at the same time,
#. asking which of the two the user wants.
#: UI/YouTube/LinkKindDialog.cs:25
msgid ""
"This address points to one video and also includes a playlist. Choose which "
"content Luna should open."
msgstr ""
"Esta dirección apunta a un video y también incluye una lista de "
"reproducción. Elige qué contenido debe abrir Luna."

#. Translators: Button that plays the one video a link names, rather than the playlist it also names.
#. Translators: One of the choices for a link naming both: always play the single video.
#: UI/YouTube/LinkKindDialog.cs:28 UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:74
msgid "Play the video"
msgstr "Reproducir el video"

#. Translators: Button that lists every video in the playlist a link names, rather than the one video.
#. Translators: One of the choices for a link naming both: always open the whole playlist.
#: UI/YouTube/LinkKindDialog.cs:31 UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:76
msgid "Open the playlist"
msgstr "Abrir la lista de reproducción"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the picture quality a video is played at.
#. Translators: Title of the window that picks the video quality a download is saved at.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:52 UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:28
msgid "Video quality"
msgstr "Calidad de video"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how many videos a search should look for.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:64
msgid "Number of search results"
msgstr "Número de resultados de búsqueda"

#. Translators: Tick box on the YouTube settings page: offer search suggestions as the user types.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:67
msgid "Show search suggestions while typing"
msgstr "Mostrar sugerencias de búsqueda al escribir"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses what to do with a link naming a video and a playlist at once.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:69
msgid "Video+playlist link behavior"
msgstr "Comportamiento al abrir enlaces de video+lista de reproducción"

#. Translators: One of the choices for a link naming both: ask which was meant, every time.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:72
msgid "Ask every time"
msgstr "Preguntar siempre"

#. Translators: Heading of the group of settings that give YouTube the browser cookies it may need.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:82
msgid "Cookies"
msgstr "Cookies"

#. Translators: Label of the box showing the cookie file yt-dlp will use, if one was chosen.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:84
msgid "Cookie file"
msgstr "Archivo de cookies"

#. Translators: Button that switches Luna to reading cookies straight from Firefox each time, with no file.
#. "Firefox" is a program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:91
msgid "Import from Firefox"
msgstr "Importar desde Firefox"

#. Translators: Label of the read-only box that says which cookie source is in use.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:96
msgid "Cookie status"
msgstr "Estado de las cookies"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses which line of yt-dlp releases to follow. "yt-dlp" is a
#. program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:117
msgid "yt-dlp update channel"
msgstr "Canal de actualización de yt-dlp"

#. Translators: One of the yt-dlp release lines: the tested one.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:120
msgid "Stable"
msgstr "Estable"

#. Translators: One of the yt-dlp release lines: rebuilt every night.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:122
msgid "Nightly"
msgstr "Nightly"

#. Translators: One of the yt-dlp release lines: rebuilt from the latest source.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:124
msgid "Master"
msgstr "Master"

#. Translators: Tick box on the YouTube settings page: look for a newer yt-dlp each time the player starts.
#. "yt-dlp" is a program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:127
msgid "Check for yt-dlp updates on startup"
msgstr "Buscar actualizaciones de yt-dlp al iniciar"

#. Translators: Button on the YouTube settings page that fetches the extra programs YouTube downloads need.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:129
msgid "Download YouTube components"
msgstr "Descargar componentes de YouTube"

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses the picture quality a video is played at.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:146
msgid ""
"Sets the picture height Luna asks for when you play a video with Enter. A "
"lower height starts sooner and uses less network; Luna falls back to the "
"closest the video offers."
msgstr ""
"Define la altura de la imagen que Luna solicita cuando reproduces un vídeo "
"con Enter. Una altura menor inicia antes y usa menos red; Luna recurrirá a "
"la opción disponible más cercana en el vídeo."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses the sound quality a video's audio is played at.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:149
msgid ""
"Sets the bitrate Luna asks for when you play a video's sound alone with "
"Ctrl+Enter. Luna falls back to the closest the video offers."
msgstr ""
"Define la tasa de bits que Luna solicita cuando reproduces solo el sonido de "
"un vídeo con Ctrl+Enter. Luna recurrirá a la opción disponible más cercana "
"en el vídeo."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how many videos a search should look for. The two numbers are
#. the smallest and largest it accepts.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:153
msgid ""
"Sets the size of the first result page, from 5 through 100 videos. Larger "
"pages take longer to fetch; reaching the end still loads more results."
msgstr ""
"Establece el tamaño de la primera página de resultados, de 5 a 100 videos. "
"Las páginas más grandes tardan más en obtenerse; llegar al final sigue "
"cargando más resultados."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that offers search suggestions while typing.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:156
msgid ""
"Offers a list of completions as you type in the search box, fetched from "
"YouTube. Clear this option to type without those background network requests."
msgstr ""
"Ofrece una lista de sugerencias a medida que escribes en el cuadro de "
"búsqueda, obtenidas de YouTube. Desactiva esta opción para escribir sin "
"realizar esas solicitudes de red en segundo plano."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses what to do with a link naming a video and a playlist at once.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:159
msgid ""
"For an address containing both a video and a playlist, Luna can ask each "
"time, open only that video, or list the complete playlist."
msgstr ""
"Para una dirección que contiene tanto un video como una lista de "
"reproducción, Luna puede preguntar cada vez, abrir solo ese video o listar "
"la lista de reproducción completa."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses which line of yt-dlp releases to follow. "yt-dlp" is a program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:162
msgid ""
"Stable changes least often and is intended for normal use. Nightly is "
"rebuilt each night. Master follows the newest source and may be unreliable."
msgstr ""
"Estable cambia con menos frecuencia y está destinada al uso normal. Nightly "
"se recompila cada noche. Master sigue el código fuente más reciente y puede "
"ser inestable."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that looks for a newer yt-dlp at startup. "yt-dlp" is a program
#. name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:166
msgid ""
"Looks for a newer yt-dlp in the background when Luna starts and offers to "
"download it. Clear this option to avoid that startup network request."
msgstr ""
"Busca una versión más reciente de yt-dlp en segundo plano al iniciar Luna y "
"ofrece descargarla. Desmarca esta opción para evitar esa solicitud de red al "
"inicio."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that fetches the extra programs YouTube downloads need. "yt-dlp" is
#. a program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:170
msgid ""
"Fetches yt-dlp and the JavaScript runtime it needs. YouTube playback and "
"downloads do not work until these are installed."
msgstr ""
"Descarga yt-dlp y el entorno de ejecución de JavaScript necesario. La "
"reproducción y descarga de YouTube no funcionarán hasta que estén instalados."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the cookie file yt-dlp will use.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:173
msgid ""
"The cookie file, in Netscape format, that YouTube requests are sent with. "
"Use it for age-restricted or members-only videos. Choosing a file turns off "
"reading cookies from Firefox."
msgstr ""
"El archivo de cookies, en formato Netscape, con el que se envían las "
"solicitudes de YouTube. Úsalo para vídeos con restricción de edad o "
"exclusivos para miembros. Seleccionar un archivo desactiva la lectura de "
"cookies desde Firefox."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that picks a cookie file by hand.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:176
msgid ""
"Opens a file picker to choose a cookie file saved from your browser. This "
"turns off reading cookies from Firefox."
msgstr ""
"Abre un explorador de archivos para elegir un archivo de cookies guardado "
"desde tu navegador. Esto desactiva la lectura de cookies desde Firefox."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that switches to reading cookies from Firefox. "Firefox" is a
#. program name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:180
msgid ""
"Reads cookies straight from Firefox each time, always up to date, with no "
"file to keep. This clears any cookie file you chose. Firefox must be "
"installed and signed in to YouTube."
msgstr ""
"Lee las cookies directamente desde Firefox cada vez, siempre actualizadas y "
"sin necesidad de conservar un archivo. Esto borra cualquier archivo de "
"cookies que hayas elegido. Firefox debe estar instalado y con la sesión "
"iniciada en YouTube."

#. Translators: Help text for the read-only box that reports which cookie source is in use.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:183
msgid ""
"Reports whether YouTube requests currently use Firefox cookies, a cookie "
"file, or no cookies at all."
msgstr ""
"Informa si las solicitudes de YouTube utilizan actualmente cookies de "
"Firefox, un archivo de cookies o ninguna cookie."

#. Translators: Cookie status: Luna is reading cookies straight from Firefox. "Firefox" is a program
#. name and is not translated.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:222
msgid "Using Firefox cookies"
msgstr "Usando cookies de Firefox"

#. Translators: Cookie status naming the file in use. {path} is a file path.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:225
msgid "Using cookie file: {path}"
msgstr "Usando archivo de cookies: {path}"

#. Translators: Cookie status: no cookies are sent with YouTube requests.
#: UI/YouTube/Preferences.cs:227
msgid "No cookies"
msgstr "Sin cookies"

#. Translators: Prompt above the list of audio bitrates to choose from when downloading.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:35
msgid "Choose the audio quality to download:"
msgstr "Selecciona la calidad de audio a descargar:"

#. Translators: Prompt above the list of video qualities to choose from when downloading.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:37
msgid "Choose the video quality to download:"
msgstr "Selecciona la calidad de vídeo a descargar:"

#. Translators: Description of the 144p video quality.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:96
msgid "144p (very low quality)"
msgstr "144p (calidad muy baja)"

#. Translators: Description of the 240p video quality.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:98
msgid "240p (low quality)"
msgstr "240p (calidad baja)"

#. Translators: Description of the 360p video quality.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:100
msgid "360p (medium quality)"
msgstr "360p (calidad media)"

#. Translators: Description of the 480p video quality.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:102
msgid "480p (medium quality)"
msgstr "480p (calidad media)"

#. Translators: Description of the 720p video quality (high definition).
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:104
msgid "720p (HD)"
msgstr "720p (HD)"

#. Translators: Description of the 1080p video quality (full high definition).
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:106
msgid "1080p (Full HD)"
msgstr "1080p (Full HD)"

#. Translators: Description of the 1440p video quality (2K).
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:108
msgid "1440p (2K)"
msgstr "1440p (2K)"

#. Translators: Description of the 2160p video quality (4K).
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:110
msgid "2160p (4K)"
msgstr "2160p (4K)"

#. Translators: A video quality with no set description. {height} is a number of pixels.
#: UI/YouTube/QualitySelectionDialog.cs:112
msgid "{height}p"
msgstr "{height}p"

#. Translators: Button that plays only the sound of the video chosen in the list, with no picture.
#: UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:174
msgid "Play as audio"
msgstr "Reproducir como audio"

#. Translators: Button that saves the video chosen in the list of results to a folder on this computer.
#. Translators: Context menu item in the results list that saves the chosen video to this computer.
#: UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:177 UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:373
msgid "Download"
msgstr "Descargar"

#. Translators: Names who published a result. {author} is a channel name.
#: UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:322 UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:339
msgid "by {author}"
msgstr "de {author}"

#. Translators: How many videos a playlist holds. {count} is a number.
#: UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:325 UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:333
msgid "contains {count} videos"
msgstr "contiene {count} vídeos"

#. Translators: Marks a row in the results list as a channel rather than a single video.
#. Translators: Heading above a YouTube channel's browser when the channel's name is not known.
#: UI/YouTube/ResultsDialog.cs:329 YouTube/Session.cs:104
msgid "Channel"
msgstr "Canal"

#. Translators: Label of the box where the user types what to search YouTube for.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:53
msgid "Search for"
msgstr "Buscar"

#. Translators: Label of the list of search suggestions that appears as the user types.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:57
msgid "Suggestions"
msgstr "Sugerencias"

#. Translators: Label of the list that narrows a YouTube search to one kind of result.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:63
msgid "Filter"
msgstr "Filtro"

#. Translators: Search filter: return results of every kind, unfiltered.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:66
msgid "No filter"
msgstr "Sin filtro"

#. Translators: Search filter: order results by when they were uploaded, newest first.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:70
msgid "Upload date"
msgstr "Fecha de subida"

#. Translators: Search filter: order results by how many times they have been viewed.
#: UI/YouTube/SearchDialog.cs:72
msgid "View count"
msgstr "Número de visualizaciones"

#. Translators: Shown when something needs the extra programs for yt-dlp and they are not installed.
#: YouTube/Backend.cs:179
msgid "YouTube components are missing."
msgstr "Faltan componentes de YouTube."

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the channel's front page.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:26
msgid "Home"
msgstr "Inicio"

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the channel's ordinary videos.
#. Translators: Title of the window listing the videos a search or a playlist turned up.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:28 YouTube/Sessions.cs:438
msgid "Videos"
msgstr "Videos"

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the channel's short vertical videos.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:30
msgid "Shorts"
msgstr "Shorts"

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the channel's live streams and their recordings.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:32
msgid "Streams"
msgstr "Transmisiones en directo"

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the playlists the channel publishes.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:34
msgid "Playlists"
msgstr "Listas de reproducción"

#. Translators: A channel browser tab: the channel's community posts.
#: YouTube/ChannelTabs.cs:36
msgid "Community"
msgstr "Comunidad"

#. Translators: Shown when the extra programs YouTube's yt-dlp support needs are already there.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:90
msgid "YouTube components are already installed."
msgstr "Los componentes de YouTube ya están instalados."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while the extra programs for yt-dlp are being fetched.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:98
msgid "Downloading YouTube components"
msgstr "Descargando componentes de YouTube"

#. Translators: First message shown while the extra programs for yt-dlp are being fetched.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:100
msgid "Contacting the download site..."
msgstr "Contactando con el sitio de descarga..."

#. Translators: Progress heading while an extra program is being fetched. {name} is the
#. program and its version, {step} which one it is and {total} how many there are.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:104
msgid "Downloading {name}, {step} of {total}"
msgstr "Descargando {name}, {step} de {total}"

#. Translators: Shown once the extra programs for yt-dlp have been fetched.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:114
msgid "YouTube components were downloaded successfully."
msgstr "Los componentes de YouTube se descargaron con éxito."

#: YouTube/Components.cs:122 YouTube/Components.cs:123
msgid "Could not install YouTube components."
msgstr "No se pudieron instalar los componentes de YouTube."

#. Translators: Shown when the user asks to update yt-dlp and it has not been installed.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:141
msgid "yt-dlp is not installed yet."
msgstr "yt-dlp aún no está instalado."

#. Translators: Spoken when the user asks to update yt-dlp.
#. Translators: The short wording spoken when the user asks to update yt-dlp.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:147 YouTube/Components.cs:149
msgid "Updating yt-dlp..."
msgstr "Actualizando yt-dlp..."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while yt-dlp is updating itself.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:152
msgid "Updating yt-dlp"
msgstr "Actualización de yt-dlp"

#. Translators: First message shown while yt-dlp is updating itself.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:154
msgid "Checking current yt-dlp version..."
msgstr "Comprobando la versión actual de yt-dlp..."

#: YouTube/Components.cs:203
msgid ""
"A newer yt-dlp version is available on the '{channel}' channel.\n"
"Current version: {current}\n"
"Latest version: {latest}\n"
"\n"
"Do you want to update now?"
msgstr ""
"Hay una nueva versión de yt-dlp disponible en el canal '{channel}'.\n"
"Versión actual: {current}\n"
"Última versión: {latest}\n"
"\n"
"¿Deseas actualizar ahora?"

#. Translators: Shown when yt-dlp could not update itself and said nothing useful about why.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:261
msgid "Could not update yt-dlp."
msgstr "No se pudo actualizar yt-dlp."

#. Translators: Stands in for a version number that could not be read.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:266
msgid "unknown"
msgstr "desconocido"

#. Translators: Shown once yt-dlp has updated itself. {old} and {new} are version numbers and
#. {channel} is the release line being followed.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:271
msgid "yt-dlp updated from {old} to {new} on the '{channel}' channel."
msgstr "yt-dlp se actualizó de {old} a {new} en el canal '{channel}'."

#. Translators: Shown when yt-dlp was already the newest build. {version} is its version number
#. and {channel} is the release line being followed.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:277
msgid "yt-dlp is already up to date ({version}) on the '{channel}' channel."
msgstr "yt-dlp ya está actualizado ({version}) en el canal '{channel}'."

#: YouTube/Components.cs:294
msgid ""
"Total size: {total}\n"
"Downloaded: {got}\n"
"Percentage: {percent}%"
msgstr ""
"Tamaño total: {total}\n"
"Descargado: {got}\n"
"Porcentaje: {percent}%"

#. Translators: Title of the messages shown about the extra programs YouTube's yt-dlp support needs.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:325
msgid "YouTube components"
msgstr "Componentes de YouTube"

#. Translators: Title of the messages shown about updating yt-dlp. "yt-dlp" is a program name and is
#. not translated.
#: YouTube/Components.cs:330
msgid "yt-dlp update"
msgstr "Actualización de yt-dlp"

#. Translators: Heading above the list of videos a YouTube search found.
#: YouTube/Session.cs:99
msgid "Search results"
msgstr "Resultados de búsqueda"

#. Translators: Heading above the list of videos in a YouTube playlist.
#: YouTube/Session.cs:106
msgid "Playlist videos"
msgstr "Videos de la lista de reproducción"

#. Translators: Message shown while the first video of a search is being made ready to play.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:127
msgid "Fetching first stream..."
msgstr "Obteniendo la primera transmisión..."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while a YouTube search is running.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:130
msgid "Searching YouTube"
msgstr "Buscando en YouTube"

#. Translators: First message shown while a YouTube search is running.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:132
msgid "Searching videos..."
msgstr "Buscando videos..."

#. Translators: Shown when a YouTube search failed and nothing said why.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:144
msgid "Could not complete YouTube search."
msgstr "No se pudo completar la búsqueda en YouTube."

#. Translators: Shown when a YouTube search found nothing at all.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:151
msgid "No videos were found for this search."
msgstr "No se encontraron videos para esta búsqueda."

#. Translators: Shown when an address looked like a YouTube link but names no playlist.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:170
msgid "This link does not include a YouTube playlist."
msgstr "Este enlace no incluye una lista de reproducción de YouTube."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while a YouTube playlist is being read.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:177
msgid "Loading YouTube link"
msgstr "Cargando enlace de YouTube"

#. Translators: First message shown while the videos in a YouTube playlist are being listed.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:179
msgid "Loading playlist items..."
msgstr "Cargando elementos de la lista de reproducción..."

#. Translators: Shown when a YouTube address could not be read and nothing said why.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:191
msgid "Could not read YouTube link data."
msgstr "No se pudieron leer los datos del enlace de YouTube."

#. Translators: Shown when a YouTube playlist address opened nothing playable.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:198
msgid "No videos were found in this playlist."
msgstr "No se encontraron videos en esta lista de reproducción."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while a YouTube channel is being opened.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:227
msgid "Loading channel"
msgstr "Cargando canal"

#. Translators: First message shown while a YouTube channel is being opened.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:229
msgid "Loading channel videos..."
msgstr "Cargando vídeos del canal..."

#. Translators: Shown when a YouTube channel could not be read.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:241
msgid "Could not read this YouTube channel."
msgstr "No se pudo leer este canal de YouTube."

#. Translators: Spoken once a video has been taken back out of the favourites from the results list.
#. Translators: The short wording spoken once a video has been removed from the favourites.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:269 YouTube/Sessions.cs:271
msgid "Removed from favorites."
msgstr "Eliminado de favoritos."

#. Translators: Spoken when a video could not be removed from the favourites.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:277
msgid "Could not remove from favorites."
msgstr "No se pudo eliminar de favoritos."

#. Translators: Spoken once a video has been added to the favourites from the results list.
#. Translators: The short wording spoken once a video has been added to the favourites.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:286 YouTube/Sessions.cs:288
msgid "Added to favorites."
msgstr "Añadido a favoritos."

#. Translators: Spoken when a video could not be added to the favourites.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:294
msgid "Could not add to favorites."
msgstr "No se pudo añadir a favoritos."

#. Translators: Shown when an address looked like a YouTube link but names no video.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:314
msgid "This link does not include a YouTube video."
msgstr "Este enlace no incluye un video de YouTube."

#. Translators: Title of the window shown while the address of a video is being looked up.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:527
msgid "Loading YouTube stream"
msgstr "Cargando transmisión de YouTube"

#. Translators: First message shown while the address of a video is being looked up.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:529
msgid "Fetching stream URL..."
msgstr "Obteniendo URL de la transmisión..."

#. Translators: Shown when a video was found but the player could not start playing it.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:583
msgid "Could not open YouTube stream."
msgstr "No se pudo abrir la transmisión de YouTube."

#. Translators: Spoken when the video after this one is being fetched before it can be played.
#. Translators: The short wording spoken while the video after this one is being fetched.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:616 YouTube/Sessions.cs:618
msgid "Loading next video..."
msgstr "Cargando el siguiente video..."

#. Translators: Spoken when the video after this one could not be fetched, so playback stops.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:646
msgid "Could not load the next video."
msgstr "No se pudo cargar el siguiente video."

#. Translators: The short wording spoken when the next video could not be fetched.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:648
msgid "Next video failed."
msgstr "Fallo en el siguiente video."

#. Translators: Shown when a video is private, deleted, or never existed.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:748
msgid "This video is not available."
msgstr "Este video no está disponible."

#. Translators: Shown when YouTube has the video but will not serve it - age restricted, blocked
#. in this country, or paid for.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:751
msgid "YouTube will not play this video here."
msgstr "YouTube no reproducirá este video aquí."

#. Translators: Shown when a video exists but offers nothing the player can play.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:753
msgid "Could not resolve a playable stream."
msgstr "No se pudo obtener una transmisión para reproducir."

#. Translators: Shown when the programs YouTube playback needs are not installed. "yt-dlp" is a
#. program name and is not translated.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:756
msgid ""
"YouTube components are missing. Download them from the YouTube settings to "
"play or download videos."
msgstr ""
"Faltan componentes de YouTube. Descárgalos desde los ajustes de YouTube para "
"reproducir o descargar vídeos."

#. Translators: Shown when YouTube is refusing requests from this computer for the time being.
#. "HTTP 429" is the numbered error it answers with and is not translated.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:759
msgid ""
"YouTube returned HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests). Your IP may be temporarily "
"rate-limited."
msgstr ""
"YouTube devolvió el error HTTP 429 (Demasiadas solicitudes). Tu dirección IP "
"podría estar restringida temporalmente."

#. Translators: Shown when the request never reached YouTube or its answer never arrived.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:761
msgid "Could not reach YouTube. Check the network connection."
msgstr "No se pudo conectar con YouTube. Comprueba la conexión a Internet."

#. Translators: Shown when something went wrong that the player cannot explain more precisely.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:765
msgid "Could not read this video."
msgstr "No se pudo leer este video."

#. Translators: Adds the technical reason under a message about YouTube. {message} is that
#. message and {details} is the reason, which is not translated.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:771
msgid ""
"{message}\n"
"Details: {details}"
msgstr ""
"{message}\n"
"Detalles: {details}"

#. Translators: Shown when a video could not be turned into something playable and nothing said why.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:786
msgid "Could not resolve YouTube stream."
msgstr "No se pudo obtener la transmisión de YouTube."

#. Translators: Spoken when the user reaches the end of the results list and more are being fetched.
#. Translators: The short wording spoken while more search results are being fetched.
#: YouTube/Sessions.cs:886 YouTube/Sessions.cs:888
msgid "Loading more videos..."
msgstr "Cargando más videos..."

